{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "באסמיך", :translit "ba'asamecha", :gloss "in your granaries"} {:he "סמוי", :translit "samui", :gloss "hidden"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "באסמיך", :b "זהו סמוי"}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that blessing is found only in a thing hidden from the eye, deriving this from the verse 'Hashem will command the blessing with you in your storehouses' (Deuteronomy 28:8) — storehouses being concealed places (Bava Metzia 42a). A baraita on the same page states: one who comes to measure his grain should pray that the blessing rest upon it, for blessing is not found in something that is weighed or measured or counted, only in something hidden from the eye, as it says: 'Hashem will command the blessing in your storehouses.' The Ba'al HaTurim encodes this teaching via the gematria linking באסמיך to סמוי.", :sources ["Bava Metzia 42a" "Deuteronomy 28:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:a-value 133, :b-value 134, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "זהו סמוי", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "באסמיך"}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:55.137711521Z", :model "glm-5.2"}